INT. GLOBEX HOLDINGS - OPEN-PLAN OFFICE - MORNING

A sea of beige cubicles under a drop ceiling. A motivational poster of a rowing eight hangs crooked above the water cooler. A sign: SYNERGY IS OUR MIDDLE NAME.

Five employees stand at their desks, holding paper cups of lukewarm coffee, waiting.

HORATIO PEMBERTON-ADEYEMI (50s, manager, short-sleeve shirt, tie clip like a tiny sword) clears his throat by the whiteboard.

CORDELIA VANTERPOOL-OKONKWO (30s, senior analyst, silent, immaculate) stirs her coffee without drinking it.

REGGIE FITZWILLIAM (40s, sales, loud shirt, over-whitened teeth) sprawls on the corner of a desk.

BRIGITTE SOLANKI (20s, HR coordinator, lanyard heavy with badges) clutches a binder.

DESMOND "DEZ" OKAMOTO (30s, IT, headphones round his neck, three days' growth) leans against a filing cabinet, unimpressed.

Overhead, a speaker crackles.

INTERCOM (V.O.)
(female, bright)
Good morning, Globex! A reminder that today is Casual Friday, and also Mandatory Fun Day.

HORATIO
(to the room)
Okay, team. Quick huddle.

REGGIE
We are huddled.

HORATIO
Properly huddled.

CORDELIA
We're standing four feet apart.

HORATIO
Three, please.

They shuffle a foot closer. Brigitte raises her binder like a shield. Dez rolls his eyes.

HORATIO (CONT'D)
As you know, Corporate has asked us to find twelve percent in efficiencies.

REGGIE
Twelve?

BRIGITTE
It's in the memo.

REGGIE
There's a memo?

DEZ
There's always a memo.

HORATIO
I want to be clear: nobody is being let go.

CORDELIA
Good.

HORATIO
Today.

A silence. The intercom clicks.

INTERCOM (V.O.)
(female, bright)
Reminder: the Efficiency Pizza Party begins at noon in the Collaboration Zone!

BRIGITTE
(muttering)
Efficiency Pizza.

HORATIO
What was that, Brigitte?

BRIGITTE
Nothing. Nothing at all.

HORATIO
Because if there's something you'd like to share with the group...

BRIGITTE
I'd like to share that I've been here six years and I still don't know what we do.

Nobody laughs. Reggie's grin falters. Dez takes his headphones from around his neck and puts them on. Cordelia sets her coffee down on the desk with a click.

CORDELIA
We process claims.

BRIGITTE
Which claims?

CORDELIA
Claims.

HORATIO
Let's not go off-topic.

REGGIE
I sell the claims. I think.

DEZ
(removing one earphone)
You sell the claims? To whom?

REGGIE
To people who have claims.

DEZ
People with claims don't need to buy claims.

REGGIE
Dez, buddy, you don't understand sales.

DEZ
I understand there's no product.

A new figure appears at the end of the aisle. A tall man in an immaculate grey suit, hair slicked back, folder under one arm. MR. BARNABY CRANSTON-LEE (50s, regional VP, eyes like glass). The room freezes.

CRANSTON-LEE
Don't stop on my account.

HORATIO
Mr. Cranston-Lee! We didn't expect you.

CRANSTON-LEE
That is the point of the visit.

He walks down the aisle. His shoes click. He stops by Cordelia's desk and picks up her coffee. Sniffs. Sets it down.

CRANSTON-LEE (CONT'D)
Lukewarm.

CORDELIA
It's been a long morning.

CRANSTON-LEE
Of course it has.

He opens the folder. Takes out a single sheet of paper. Holds it up.

CRANSTON-LEE (CONT'D)
Twelve percent.

REGGIE
We were just discussing...

CRANSTON-LEE
I know what you were discussing. Brigitte. How many years?

BRIGITTE
Six, sir.

CRANSTON-LEE
Dez.

DEZ
Four.

CRANSTON-LEE
Cordelia.

CORDELIA
Nine.

CRANSTON-LEE
Reggie.

REGGIE
Fifteen! Fifteen glorious years, sir!

CRANSTON-LEE
Horatio.

HORATIO
(swallowing)
Twenty-two.

CRANSTON-LEE
Twenty-two years. And in that time, none of you has produced a single claim.

The intercom crackles.

INTERCOM (V.O.)
(female, bright)
Mandatory Fun Day will now begin!

Cranston-Lee lowers the page. Looks around at five stricken faces. Then, to everyone's astonishment, he smiles.

CRANSTON-LEE
Don't worry. Neither has anyone else. That's why the company's been so profitable.

HORATIO
Sir?

CRANSTON-LEE
Efficiencies, Horatio. I want twelve percent more nothing.

He tucks the folder under his arm and strides out. Nobody breathes. Reggie, slowly, raises his paper cup.

REGGIE
To nothing.

DEZ
To nothing.

CORDELIA
To nothing.

BRIGITTE
(muttering)
Efficiency pizza.

FADE OUT.
